# 17. Priority Research Questions Before Final Recommendations

Before this pillar becomes a finalized policy platform, several empirical questions should be answered.

### 17.1 Prevention

How many species identified as at-risk through State Wildlife Action Plans subsequently become federally listed?

### 17.2 Cost

What is the relative cost of:

**preventive intervention vs. intensive recovery?**

### 17.3 Monitoring

Which monitoring systems have demonstrably changed management decisions?

### 17.4 Funding

Which conservation programs experience meaningful ecological consequences from funding interruptions?

### 17.5 Coordination

Which existing interstate, federal-state, Tribal, or public-private conservation partnerships have produced measurable benefits?

### 17.6 Private lands

Which voluntary conservation mechanisms produce the greatest ecological benefit per public dollar?

### 17.7 Performance

Which indicators most reliably predict future biological improvement?

### 17.8 Workforce

Where are staffing or expertise shortages actually constraining conservation outcomes?

### 17.9 Persistence

What happens to species after delisting?

### 17.10 Institutional durability

Which conservation institutions have remained effective across major changes in administrations, budgets, and policy priorities?

